    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "unnumbered",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00324:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "The coupling of an N-protected L-alanine  and a carboxyl-protected L-leucine  ester with D C C, followed by deprotection of the protecting groups  provided the corresponding dipeptide  Ala-Leu"
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_26_07_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00003",
      "segmentId": "m00324:para:para-00003"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00002",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00324:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "Carboxyl-protection of L-leucine with either methanol or benzyl alcohol,  catalyzed by hydrochloric acid, to form the corresponding  L- leucinate esters. Deprotection with sodium hydroxide or hydrogenation regenerates the free acid."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_26_07_002.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00004",
      "segmentId": "m00324:para:para-00004"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00003",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00324:alt:fig-00003-alt",
          "text": "L-Alanine reacts with tertiary-butyl dicarbonate and triethylamine to form B o c-(L)-Ala. Alanine reacts with fluorenylmethyloxycarbonyl chloride and triethyl amine to form F m o c- (L)-Ala."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_26_07_003.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00005",
      "segmentId": "m00324:para:para-00005"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00004",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00324:alt:fig-00004-alt",
          "text": "Five steps in the synthesis of Ala-Leu. The amino group and the carboxyl group are protected. They are coupled with N, N-dicyclohexylcarbodiimide, and later deprotected to produce the dipetide, Ala-Leu."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_26_07_004.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
